From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:33:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: host: apple-a7-wlan: Take the board from match data, add
 the J85

Rename the J72 HSIC transport to apple-a7-wlan (CONFIG_APPLE_A7_WLAN)
and move its board-specific addresses into a table matched on
"apple,j72" and "apple,j85". The J72 entry carries the exact values the
J72 transport used, its J72 baselines stay enforced and its release pin
stays, so the J72 path is unchanged apart from names and added logging.
The exported helper is now apple_a7_wlan_host_ready().

The iPad mini 2 (J85) entry comes from its Apple device tree:
/arm-io/usb-complex/usb-ehci1/wlan puts the radio on EHCI1 (reg
0x400000 under usb-complex, so 0x20c400000, irq 0xa5) port 1, its HSIC
PHY at usb-complex +0x60 (0x20c000060; the J72 one is at +0x50),
host_ready on GPIO 0xa3, device_ready on 0xa4 and the reset on PMU GPIO
3, the same as the J72. The ADT pmgr device list has HSIC2_PHY (PS reg
0x20128) as the only HSIC PHY under USB2HOST1 (0x20180), matching
ps_hsic2_phy and ps_usb2host1 in s5l8960x-pmgr.dtsi. The usb_widget
offsets in the J85 ADT (+1c/3c/5c/7c of 0x20c900000) are the
ones the J72 transport reads.

The J85 register baselines are not measured. Values that only describe
the starting state (domain states, HOST_READY/DEVICE_READY pin words,
EHCI HCSPARAMS/HCCPARAMS, non-active port words, ROM revision, RAM size
and remap) are logged against the J72 measurements and the J85 path
continues. Values that a following write depends on (PHY control 4 and
config 0x153 before the PHY transition, PMU GPIO3 0x09 before the reset
release, usb_widget 0x108 for the DMA remap, EHCI caplength/version for
the fixed operational offsets) must still match: the J85 path logs them
and refuses to write when they do not. The ROM must report chip 0x4324,
as the ADT wifi-chipset says; the 0a5c:bd1c boot identity is assumed
from the J72.

On a J85, with confirm_native=1 keep_active=1, the gated
values matched, the radio came out of reset and its boot ROM enumerated
as 0a5c:bd1c on EHCI1 port 1. The J72 entry was not run again after the
change.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/host/Kconfig                      |  16 +-
 drivers/usb/host/Makefile                     |   2 +-
 .../{j72-wlan-hcd.h => apple-a7-wlan-hcd.h}   |  64 ++--
 ...72_wlan_transport_v3.c => apple-a7-wlan.c} | 342 ++++++++++++++----
 4 files changed, 318 insertions(+), 106 deletions(-)
 rename drivers/usb/host/{j72-wlan-hcd.h => apple-a7-wlan-hcd.h} (77%)
 rename drivers/usb/host/{j72_wlan_transport_v3.c => apple-a7-wlan.c} (61%)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/Kconfig b/drivers/usb/host/Kconfig
index 678258c36..e8e0e8013 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/host/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/Kconfig
@@ -734,10 +734,16 @@ config USB_XEN_HCD
 	  Only needed if the kernel is running in a Xen guest and generic
 	  access to a USB device is needed.
 
-config J72_WLAN_TRANSPORT
-	tristate "Opt-in J72 internal HSIC Wi-Fi transport"
+config APPLE_A7_WLAN
+	tristate "Apple A7 (S5L8960X) internal HSIC Wi-Fi transport"
 	depends on ARCH_APPLE && USB_EHCI_HCD && I2C && GPIOLIB && PM_GENERIC_DOMAINS
 	help
-	  Exact J72 measured PHY, radio reset, HOST_READY and EHCI ownership.
-	  Requires explicit confirm_native; checks initial hardware state and
-	  uses the normal USB HCD/DMA APIs. No automatic DT probe.
+	  Owns the HSIC PHY, radio reset, HOST_READY and the EHCI root port
+	  of the BCM43241 on the iPad Air 1 (J72) and iPad mini 2 (J85), so
+	  that brcmfmac can download its firmware over USB.
+
+	  The J72 baseline was measured on that board and is enforced. The
+	  J85 addresses come from its Apple device tree; its register
+	  baselines are unmeasured, so they are logged and any write that
+	  depends on a J72 baseline is refused unless the board matches it.
+	  Requires the confirm_native parameter; there is no DT probe.
diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/Makefile b/drivers/usb/host/Makefile
index 45ac0b2d1..bf57cebe5 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/host/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/Makefile
